Design decisions:
- Zod (not class-validator) at the API boundary via ZodValidationPipe; shared-types is type-only.
- bcryptjs (not bcrypt): no native builds, installs everywhere.
- No lockfile shipped: scaffolded projects generate + commit their own pnpm-lock.yaml.
- Placeholder: __PROJECT_SLUG__ (package names + titles), replaced by scripts/scaffold.sh.
- Tier-2 (queue/storage/worker) is opt-in: not imported by AppModule, redis/worker only
  start under `docker compose --profile tier2`. Queue/storage driver logic lives once in
  packages/queue-core + packages/storage-core (DRY) — apps/api wraps them as NestJS
  modules, apps/worker consumes them directly (no NestJS dependency for a background job
  runner). Job payload contract fixed in queue-core/job-types.ts (transcode today).
- queue-core/storage-core ship REAL runtime exports (unlike shared-types, which is
  type-only) — so unlike shared-types they have their own `build`+`postinstall` (tsc ->
  dist/) and `main`/`types` point at `dist`, not `src`. Without this, a compiled
  `node dist/main.js` in production cannot resolve the raw `.ts` workspace package (Node's
  own module resolver, not a bundler); `postinstall` guarantees `dist/` exists right after
  `pnpm install`, before typecheck/test/build ever run, so CI's lint->typecheck->test->build
  order needs no change.

